<title>SINGAPORE: SSL in US$40 mln Vietnam venture.</title>
<headline>SSL in US$40 mln Vietnam venture.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Property-based Straits Steamship Land Ltd (SSL) said on Thursday it has entered into a US$40 million venture to build a 22-storey apartment block in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement it would hold a 60 percent stake in the development with the Vietnamese state-owned enterprise, Army Garment Import Export Company, holding the remaining 40 percent.</p>
<p>It said the proposed apartment block of 2,808 square metres would be on Thai Van Lung Street in Ho Chi Minh City's prime district.</p>
<p>Construction will start early 1997 and is expected to be completed by third quarter 1998.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
